BRIEF DESCRIPTION OF THE DRAWINGS
[0010] Referring now to the drawings in which like reference numbers represent corresponding parts throughout:
[0011] FIG. 1 illustrates a top down view of a robot platform that can be used to carry bins and assist with other tasks around an orchard in accordance with one or more embodiments of the invention;
[0012] FIG. 2 illustrates a side view of a robot platform that can be used to carry bins and assist with other tasks around an orchard in accordance with one or more embodiments of the invention;
[0013] FIG. 3 shows an alternative version of a robot and allows the carrying of multiple bins in accordance with one or more embodiments of the invention;
[0014] FIG. 4 shows a drone that can be used to perform various operations/tasks in an orchard in accordance with one or more embodiments of the invention;
[0015] FIG. 5 illustrates a swarm algorithm for managing an orchard in accordance with one or more embodiments of the invention;
[0016] FIG. 6 illustrates the logical flow for data amalgamation in accordance with one or more embodiments of the invention;
[0017] FIG. 7 illustrates a pruning algorithm for acquiring an optimal tree structure in accordance with one or more embodiments of the invention;
[0018] FIGS. 8A-8P illustrate exemplary sandboxes that reflect various exemplary stages of an orchard in accordance with one or more embodiments of the invention;
[0019] FIG. 9 illustrates the flow and further details for Task Division and Task Allocation in accordance with one or more embodiments of the invention;
[0020] FIG. 10 illustrates the logical flow for managing an orchard in accordance with one or more embodiments of the invention;
[0021] FIG. 11 is an exemplary hardware and software environment used to implement one or more embodiments of the invention; and
[0022] FIG. 12 schematically illustrates a typical distributed/cloud-based computer system in accordance with one or more embodiments of the invention.
